    "created_at": "2018-03-12T21:44:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-12T21:44:37Z",
    "body": "If you can ensure the out-of-bounds pointer won't be live for more than an instruction or two, it might be okay to mark those as unsafe points. We're absolutely going to need unsafe points for the write barrier, but I've been working on removing them from other compiler constructs (like range loops).",
